# `files` in package.json is the allowlist; this file is the subtractive pass that
# runs *inside* those directories. Both are needed: an allowlisted directory ships
# whole, and `.gitignore` is not consulted once `files` is present — so anything
# untracked that happens to sit under scripts/ or skills/ would otherwise be packed.
# That is not hypothetical: OMC HUD state (absolute paths, session ids) had
# accumulated under scripts/facebook/ and scripts/instagram/ and made it into a
# `npm pack` listing. Re-run `npm pack` and read the file list before every publish.

# Agent/session state — carries local absolute paths and session ids
.omc/
.claude-project/
.claude/

# User state and secrets — never leaves the machine
.env
*.env
!.env.example
browser-profile/
profile/
posts/
published*.json
queue.json
*-cache.json
ledgers/

# Build and editor noise
node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store
_workspace/
